# yosys gate/FF-counting script (uses the slang frontend plugin, since the
# built-in read_verilog -sv frontend chokes on some SystemVerilog
# assignment-pattern syntax emitted by firtool/CIRCT).
# Placeholders: @FILELIST@ @TOP@ @OUTDIR@ @TAG@
#
# read_slang fully elaborates the design (module hierarchy is dissolved into
# one flat top module -- this plugin does not support -keep-hierarchy), so
# `stat` immediately after gives a generic-cell (RTLIL) netlist count: this
# IS our gate/FF count, at the same abstraction level FIRRTL/CIRCT emitted.
# We deliberately do NOT run the full `synth -flatten` optimization+techmap
# recipe: on this ~260k-cell/10M-wire-bit flat netlist its CHECK pass hung
# for >9 minutes with zero progress on this shared host (see logs/*_heavy_synth_killed.log)
# and was abandoned as not worth the runtime for a same-methodology delta
# comparison. Both configs are measured with the identical (lean) recipe, so
# the control vs WideMbus delta is still apples-to-apples.
#
# SRAM *_ext macros are true RTL blackboxes in the source (no body anywhere
# in gen-collateral) -- their area was already characterized separately with
# CACTI, so they naturally stay as blackbox cells and contribute 0 further
# gates/FFs here. -D SYNTHESIS selects the synthesizable branch of
# plusarg_reader.v (assign out = DEFAULT) instead of the sim-only
# $value$plusargs branch.
plugin -i slang
read_slang -f @FILELIST@ -D SYNTHESIS --top @TOP@

tee -o @OUTDIR@/@TAG@.generic_stat.txt stat -top @TOP@
